{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011Cgj424sHw6PEEd2MdGADk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"*The door stands before you — ancient, weathered oak bound with iron. At the word \"key,\" a deep resonance hums through the grain of the wood. The iron bands glow faintly, rust flaking away to reveal symbols beneath.*\n\n*A keyhole appears where none was before — not a simple opening, but a void that seems to breathe, pulling light inward at its edges.*\n\n*The door speaks, not with sound, but with the creak of its own weight shifting:*\n\n**You said the word. But you did not bring the thing.**\n\n**A key is not a key when it is only spoken. It must be turned. It must fit. It must know the shape of what it opens.**\n\n**What do you wish to unlock?**\n\n*The keyhole waits. The hinges hold. The door is listening.*"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":41,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":187,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}